    dict(key='19-act-5-figure', kind='figure', title='How deep, how long: the limits on the stream',
         body='stream_limits',
         narration="Fifth demo: limits on the stream. [[slnc 400]] On the left, three limits. [[slnc 300]] How deep the J S O N may nest. [[slnc 300]] How long a text may be. [[slnc 300]] And how many digits a number may have. [[slnc 600]] Jackson three's defaults are generous: five hundred levels, a hundred million characters, a thousand digits. [[slnc 300]] The request mapper tightens them to what a cart needs: ten levels, sixty-four characters, ten digits. [[slnc 700]] On the right, the inputs. [[slnc 300]] Five thousand levels is refused even by the default. [[slnc 300]] Eleven levels, a sixty-five character product code, and an eleven digit quantity are refused by the tightened limits. [[slnc 600]] Limits protect memory and the stack, whatever the types."),
